Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\[Chi]\.b2 Comparison", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977140550838667*^9, 
  3.9771405531982822`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ee4b68dc-8d43-459e-8704-\
13ed383a551c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To quantify model performance, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[Chi]", "2"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a457e95a-74ff-7b4c-9a41-39fad052fe45"],
 " values are computed from the covariance-weighted residuals using the full \
STAT+SYS matrix."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977140561245487*^9, 3.9771405953866787`*^9}, {
  3.9772557550990067`*^9, 3.977255791070303*^9}, {3.977256080169689*^9, 
  3.977256081786312*^9}, {3.9800887012037086`*^9, 
  3.980088731727186*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6dde6783-5856-8c42-9fb2-\
1885fc00f3f9"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"chi2FromResiduals", "[", "res_", "]"}], ":=", 
   RowBox[{"res", ".", 
    RowBox[{"LinearSolve", "[", 
     RowBox[{"supernovaCovarianceMatrix", ",", "res"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"chi2PME", "=", 
   RowBox[{"chi2FromResiduals", "[", "pmeResiduals", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"chi2FLRW", "=", 
   RowBox[{"chi2FromResiduals", "[", "flrwResiduals", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"redChi2PME", "=", 
   RowBox[{"chi2PME", "/", 
    RowBox[{"Length", "[", "supernovaRedshifts", "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"redChi2FLRW", "=", 
   RowBox[{"chi2FLRW", "/", 
    RowBox[{"Length", "[", "supernovaRedshifts", "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"Grid", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Model\>\"", 
       ",", "\"\<\!\(\*SuperscriptBox[\(\[Chi]\), \(2\)]\)\>\"", 
       ",", "\"\<\!\(\*SubsuperscriptBox[\(\[Chi]\), \(red\), \(2\)]\)\>\""}],
       "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<PME\>\"", ",", "chi2PME", ",", "redChi2PME"}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<FLRW\>\"", ",", "chi2FLRW", ",", "redChi2FLRW"}], "}"}]}], 
    "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", "->", "All"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"ItemStyle", "->", "12"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9770818421702595`*^9, 3.9770818421702595`*^9}, {
   3.9770819104448185`*^9, 3.977081933825239*^9}, 3.9771343749621506`*^9, {
   3.977134412661524*^9, 3.9771344273694763`*^9}, {3.9771406033904114`*^9, 
   3.977140604214319*^9}, 3.977140690761402*^9, {3.9771407263696156`*^9, 
   3.9771407361055355`*^9}, {3.977147205052868*^9, 3.9771472413394012`*^9}, {
   3.977238422332897*^9, 3.9772384364346485`*^9}, {3.9772398671128063`*^9, 
   3.977239877299721*^9}, {3.9772401405860405`*^9, 3.9772401559943333`*^9}, {
   3.9797405904280434`*^9, 3.979740622530922*^9}, {3.9797406895631256`*^9, 
   3.979740694272833*^9}, {3.979740737546566*^9, 3.979740738293867*^9}, {
   3.979740781173359*^9, 3.9797408358357983`*^9}, {3.9835153233749065`*^9, 
   3.983515333695795*^9}, {3.9835153975223866`*^9, 3.9835154025219193`*^9}, {
   3.9835161490774956`*^9, 3.983516200226967*^9}, {3.983523656504076*^9, 
   3.983523657002514*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[177]:=",ExpressionUUID->"198ae807-84a8-4c06-b09e-3f7147ae0d90"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {"\<\"Model\"\>", "\<\"\\!\\(\\*SuperscriptBox[\\(\[Chi]\\), \
\\(2\\)]\\)\"\>", "\<\"\\!\\(\\*SubsuperscriptBox[\\(\[Chi]\\), \\(red\\), \
\\(2\\)]\\)\"\>"},
    {"\<\"PME\"\>", "2726.501496641154`", "1.678880231921893`"},
    {"\<\"FLRW\"\>", "4049.2432662494703`", "2.493376395473812`"}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxItemStyle->{"Columns" -> {{12}}, "Rows" -> {{12}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9868209027056465`*^9, 3.9891499215746136`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[182]=",ExpressionUUID->"fb842f82-b6fb-a640-bca3-bdfc33ee7780"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both models reproduce the overall distance\[Dash]redshift trend in the \
Pantheon+ data. The fixed-parameter FLRW reference yields a lower ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[Chi]", "2"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "1841232c-2e11-254f-a36a-404c3e24c93d"],
 ", while PME achieves a one-parameter kinematic fit once the acceleration \
scale is externally fixed by the BTFR."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9797410622285175`*^9, 3.9797411365772476`*^9}, {
   3.980088741035698*^9, 3.9800887685255604`*^9}, 3.9801579687360935`*^9, 
   3.980158055408844*^9, 3.9803639921806755`*^9, {3.9803647570088863`*^9, 
   3.98036477177903*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bfcf7b93-3846-da4e-b1d4-\
9dc5f3483226"],

Cell["\<\
However, the difference is structural, not numeric. In FLRW, the expansion \
history is governed primarily by free density parameters. In PME, the same \
large-scale behavior is a direct consequence of the manifold kinematics.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9801579978579865`*^9, {3.980281262961708*^9, 3.980281264352188*^9}, {
   3.98028132477516*^9, 3.98028132627487*^9}, {3.980363999226019*^9, 
   3.980364015008028*^9}, {3.9803647947892056`*^9, 3.980364824571062*^9}, {
   3.9803648762738457`*^9, 3.9803648931862564`*^9}, 3.980365686117073*^9, 
   3.981804750128851*^9},ExpressionUUID->"d968cb60-e9be-9f43-ae66-\
321b5ed88b85"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Conclusion", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.979408374796034*^9, 
  3.9794083769420185`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a6982fe4-2147-4e87-ab6d-\
1887b58d0d5c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In this work we have presented a reconstruction of gravitational dynamics \
grounded in kinematics rather than force, curvature, or action at a distance. \
Within the Parabolic Expansion Model, a universal kinematic deceleration of \
fixed magnitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["A", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "3de2b063-f3ee-9d4c-9bdd-4ac1987f861e"],
 " emerges as a global property of the manifold. Acceleration Flux Theory \
identifies this deceleration as a conserved bilocal quantity that exists \
independently of matter and persists across all scales."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.979408384074049*^9, 3.9794084300890884`*^9}, 
   3.9795649721496487`*^9, {3.981726533143715*^9, 
   3.98172654148543*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bdce6192-0b37-4344-a7d0-\
57a38018355a"],

Cell["\<\
Matter does not generate gravitational acceleration, nor does it deform \
spacetime. Instead, baryonic structure redistributes an ambient background \
acceleration scale, concentrating flux and producing spatial gradients. In \
the local bound regime this redistribution yields an inhomogeneous \
acceleration component obeying a Gauss-type constraint that reproduces the \
familiar inverse-square behavior associated with Newtonian gravity. The \
resulting local acceleration,\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9794084413139095`*^9, 3.9794084756374226`*^9}, 
   3.9795649347986984`*^9, 
   3.9817265513867073`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"29d8a3d6-4615-7a43-ad32-\
bfc9eeb9e5ce"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["a", "in"], "(", "r", ")"}], "=", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "A"}], "-", 
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{"GM", "(", "r", ")"}], 
       SuperscriptBox["r", "2"]]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
   "33e81b21-34bc-1549-ab0a-ef85317fb324"]],ExpressionUUID->
   "90d1ca93-d913-494d-bac1-6a5529173fd7"], ","}]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9793992013571815`*^9, 
  3.979399249519516*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0c7abb06-13b5-6c45-870f-\
3d035b191550"],

Cell["\<\
arises without invoking forces, potentials, or nonlocal interactions.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9794085182933846`*^9, 
  3.9794085353432465`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"cda89ede-760a-a146-a87a-\
d3d614f0755e"],

Cell["\<\
Within this framework, momentum is not exchanged through forces acting \
between distant bodies. Momentum change is the local, observable response of \
mass to a structured acceleration flux. Newton\[CloseCurlyQuote]s second law \
is retained operationally but reinterpreted: it describes how matter couples \
to an existing background acceleration scale rather than how bodies exert \
forces upon one another. Conservation of momentum follows from conservation \
of acceleration flux under redistribution, replacing action\[Dash]reaction \
pairs with flux balance.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9794085419142056`*^9, 3.9794085930119057`*^9}, 
   3.9794090693614826`*^9, 3.9795649364862747`*^9, 3.979564991970207*^9, 
   3.98172656686817*^9},ExpressionUUID->"78278b08-50cc-b944-8c25-\
3f40ce4af834"],

Cell["\<\
This construction resolves a long-standing conceptual tension in classical \
gravity. Newton\[CloseCurlyQuote]s laws successfully describe motion but \
provide no physical account of how gravitational influence is transmitted. \
Acceleration Flux Theory supplies that missing mechanism while preserving the \
empirical content of Newtonian dynamics. In doing so it also exposes the \
limitation of Newton\[CloseCurlyQuote]s first law: inertial motion is not \
fundamental but an approximation that neglects a universal background \
acceleration. Objects at rest do not remain at rest; they evolve under a \
persistent kinematic acceleration scale whose effects appear once \
acceleration is treated as primary.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.979408608558758*^9, 3.979408633121153*^9}, {
   3.9794086825229855`*^9, 3.979408709793829*^9}, {3.9794090803400993`*^9, 
   3.9794090889493446`*^9}, {3.979563444345684*^9, 3.979563454502121*^9}, {
   3.979565656221077*^9, 3.9795656623003864`*^9}, 
   3.9817265769169617`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"ed73ce23-f036-9a47-9acc-\
f0fcbb416953"],

Cell["\<\
Gravity therefore emerges not as a force and not as geometry, but as the \
organized redistribution of a conserved background acceleration scale. The \
same kinematic structure that governs cosmic expansion also governs local \
attraction, unifying gravitational phenomena across scales without additional \
assumptions or dark sectors. Acceleration Flux Theory thus provides a \
physically intelligible, local, and deterministic foundation for gravity\
\[LongDash]one that resolves several longstanding conceptual difficulties, \
including action at a distance, dynamical spacetime curvature, and the \
separation between cosmic expansion and local gravitational attraction, while \
remaining fully compatible with observed dynamics.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.979408719324541*^9, 3.979408740855385*^9}, {
   3.9794087709182396`*^9, 3.9794087789662094`*^9}, {3.979409415966614*^9, 
   3.9794094322456875`*^9}, 3.9795649381731567`*^9, 
   3.981726606015461*^9},ExpressionUUID->"41b9b57b-7892-8e4f-accc-\
1dc15606a280"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
},
